      "file": "scenes/scene-1.js",
      "narration": "Low contrast is the most common problem, and one of the easiest to fix. Aim for four and a half to one for normal text, and three to one for large text.",
      "storyboard": "Night stage. A grey word 'Read me' fades in nearly invisible against the dark; on 'easiest to fix' it brightens to paper white. On 'four and a half to one' a giant '4.5:1' counts up at 160px in paper with a small label 'normal text'. On 'three to one' a second figure '3:1' slides in to its right in amber, labelled 'large text & key graphics'. The near-black and photo-panel bullets are cut to keep one idea; camera holds wide on the two ratios.",
      "minDuration": 11,
      "slide": {
        "title": "Contrast Is the Foundation",
        "text": "4.5:1 for normal text. 3:1 for large text and key graphics. Near-black text on light backgrounds. Panel behind text on photos",
        "notes": "Low contrast is the most common problem, and one of the easiest to fix. Aim for four and a half to one for normal text, and test with a checker.",
