      "file": "scenes/scene-3.js",
      "narration": "Some viewers can't tell red from green. Give each status a label and an icon, and let colour be an extra cue, not the only one.",
      "storyboard": "Split screen on paper. Left 'Before': two status dots in red and green; on 'can't tell red from green' both desaturate to identical muddy grey. Right 'After': on 'a label and an icon' pills read 'On track' with a tick and 'Late' with a clock, staying readable even when greyed. On 'extra cue' the colour floods back softly behind the pills. A tiny line chart with series labelled directly at line ends slides in below and holds.",
      "minDuration": 11,
      "slide": {
        "title": "Never Rely on Colour Alone",
        "text": "Before: status shown in red or green text. After: \"On track\" and \"Late\" labels plus icons. Label chart series directly",
        "notes": "Some viewers can't tell red from green. Give each status a label and an icon, and let colour be an extra cue, not the only one.",
