      "file": "scenes/scene-4.js",
      "narration": "Big, plain, left-aligned text reads well in a room and on a small screen. Body text at 24 point or larger, headlines at 36 or larger.",
      "storyboard": "Night stage, left-aligned layout with wide right margin. A tiny script-font line shrinks and blurs away on 'plain'. On '24 point' a body-text sample grows to size with a ruler tick labelled '24pt+'; on '36' the headline sample above it scales up, labelled '36pt+', in amber. A phone outline slides in on 'small screen' showing the same text still crisp. Sentence case is shown implicitly; the bullet list is cut.",
      "minDuration": 10,
      "slide": {
        "title": "Make Text Easy to Read",
        "text": "Body text 24pt or larger. Headlines 36pt or larger. Left-align body text. Use sentence case",
        "notes": "Big, plain, left-aligned text reads well in a room and on a small screen. Avoid script or very light fonts, and leave plenty of space.",
